#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "promisor.quiet"
msgstr "promisor.quiet"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:4
msgid ""
"If set to \"true\" assume `--quiet` when fetching additional objects for a "
"partial clone."
msgstr ""
"true に設定すると、 部分クローン(partial clone)の追加オブジェクトを取得"
"(fetch)するときに `--quiet` とみなします。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:5
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "promisor.quiet"
msgid "promisor.advertise"
msgstr "promisor.quiet"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:11
msgid ""
"If set to \"true\", a server will use the \"promisor-remote\" capability, "
"see linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5], to advertise the promisor remotes it is "
"using, if it uses some. Default is \"false\", which means the \"promisor-"
"remote\" capability is not advertised."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:12
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "promisor.quiet"
msgid "promisor.sendFields"
msgstr "promisor.quiet"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:19
msgid ""
"A comma or space separated list of additional remote related field names. A "
"server sends these field names and the associated field values from its "
"configuration when advertising its promisor remotes using the \"promisor-"
"remote\" capability, see linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5]. Currently, only the "
"\"partialCloneFilter\" and \"token\" field names are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "`partialCloneFilter`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:22
msgid "contains the partial clone filter used for the remote."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "`token`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:24
msgid "contains an authentication token for the remote."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:29
msgid ""
"When a field name is part of this list and a corresponding \"remote.foo."
"<field-name>\" config variable is set on the server to a non-empty value, "
"then the field name and value are sent when advertising the promisor remote "
"\"foo\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:33
msgid ""
"This list has no effect unless the \"promisor.advertise\" config variable is "
"set to \"true\", and the \"name\" and \"url\" fields are always advertised "
"regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "promisor.acceptFromServer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:53
msgid ""
"If set to \"all\", a client will accept all the promisor remotes a server "
"might advertise using the \"promisor-remote\" capability. If set to "
"\"knownName\" the client will accept promisor remotes which are already "
"configured on the client and have the same name as those advertised by the "
"client. This is not very secure, but could be used in a corporate setup "
"where servers and clients are trusted to not switch name and URLs. If set to "
"\"knownUrl\", the client will accept promisor remotes which have both the "
"same name and the same URL configured on the client as the name and URL "
"advertised by the server. This is more secure than \"all\" or \"knownName\", "
"so it should be used if possible instead of those options. Default is "
"\"none\", which means no promisor remote advertised by a server will be "
"accepted. By accepting a promisor remote, the client agrees that the server "
"might omit objects that are lazily fetchable from this promisor remote from "
"its responses to \"fetch\" and \"clone\" requests from the client. Name and "
"URL comparisons are case sensitive. See linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:54
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "promisor.quiet"
msgid "promisor.checkFields"
msgstr "promisor.quiet"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:61
msgid ""
"A comma or space separated list of additional remote related field names. A "
"client checks if the values of these fields transmitted by a server "
"correspond to the values of these fields in its own configuration before "
"accepting a promisor remote. Currently, \"partialCloneFilter\" and \"token\" "
"are the only supported field names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:65
msgid ""
"If one of these field names (e.g., \"token\") is being checked for an "
"advertised promisor remote (e.g., \"foo\"), three conditions must be met for "
"the check of this specific field to pass:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:68
msgid ""
"The corresponding local configuration (e.g., `remote.foo.token`)  must be "
"set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:69
msgid "The server must advertise the \"token\" field for remote \"foo\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:71
msgid ""
"The value of the locally configured `remote.foo.token` must exactly match "
"the value advertised by the server for the \"token\" field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:74
msgid ""
"If any of these conditions is not met for any field name listed in `promisor."
"checkFields`, the advertised remote \"foo\" is rejected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:80
msgid ""
"For the \"partialCloneFilter\" field, this allows the client to ensure that "
"the server's filter matches what it expects locally, preventing "
"inconsistencies in filtering behavior. For the \"token\" field, this can be "
"used to verify that authentication credentials match expected values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:82
msgid "Field values are compared case-sensitively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:85
msgid ""
"The \"name\" and \"url\" fields are always checked according to the "
"`promisor.acceptFromServer` policy, independently of this setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/promisor.adoc:91
msgid ""
"The field names and values should be passed by the server through the "
"\"promisor-remote\" capability by using the `promisor.sendFields` config "
"variable. The fields are checked only if the `promisor.acceptFromServer` "
"config variable is not set to \"None\". If set to \"None\", this config "
"variable has no effect. See linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5]."
msgstr ""
